Test a plausible treatment against evidence (@shoulder-treatment-evidence: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @shoulder, #source @med-source-fimpact, #source @med-source-tendinopathy-guideline, #medicine @shoulder-review, #orthopedics @shoulder-review, #shoulder @shoulder-review) { r_0Y6CMCRFXDGN20QGXNDKS55VXD
**Read a complete primary study in stages:** [FIMPACT — ten-year placebo-surgery comparison](../../../sources/FIMPACT-ten-year.lingua#r_467SRCDKYQD418N93SZG3635D8), first the structured abstract, then Methods and Results, and finally Discussion and limitations. Identify the enrolled population, comparisons, outcomes, and follow-up before reading a conclusion. Reuse [Read medical evidence and recognize its limits](../../../foundations/Evidence-and-uncertainty.lingua#r_23DWDDM1D9GY3JG0GCSS2G5B4W) for trial vocabulary.

The FIMPACT ten-year follow-up compared arthroscopic subacromial decompression with placebo surgery and exercise therapy in its defined subacromial-pain population. It reported no additional benefit of decompression over those comparisons. This challenges an apparently straightforward explanation that removing a presumed mechanical obstacle must improve this pain problem.

The result concerns that procedure, population, and comparison. It cannot be extended to every shoulder operation, acute traumatic injury, fracture treatment, instability repair, or every cuff tear. Anatomical plausibility and a patient's improvement after an intervention are insufficient on their own to establish its specific benefit.

**Study task:** reconstruct the trial question, explain what the placebo-surgery comparison contributes, inspect follow-up and uncertainty, and write a bounded conclusion. Compare it with the treatment discussion in the relevant guideline, noting publication timing and differences in scope. List what would make the evidence applicable or inapplicable to a new clinical question.

**Continue:** [Explain shoulder function and evaluate a clinical claim](Shoulder-review.lingua#r_0KVS4CSNH1J97G8XKXEW5183JW).

